<!--
  Local apps v3 (agent-driven) + AskUserQuestion card copy.

  A SEPARATE resource file on purpose: values/strings.xml is periodically
  regenerated by the cross-platform localization sync, which has already
  dropped keys the live Android code references. Everything here is either
  (a) a key that surviving code references and the sync deleted, restored
  verbatim, or (b) new v3 copy (sessions catalog, question card, task-status
  notices). Keys must stay unique against values/strings.xml — the resource
  merger fails on duplicates, which is the tripwire that tells us the sync
  re-learned one of these keys.

  The tripwire fired on 2026-08-11: the sync re-learned the create-dialog Git
  toggle, all seven runtime capability prompts, and three session-catalog keys.
  Per the rule above they were DELETED here (generated output wins), which is
  also why the "runtime capability prompts" group no longer exists.

  2026-08-24: the conversational create flow deleted the create dialog, so the
  restored create-brief label/hint went with it, and the shell kickoff string
  moved into resources/translations/*.json as local_apps_kickoff — it is now
  generated into all five values*/strings.xml and no longer lives here.
-->
